<title>UK: Premier Oil net jumps 87 pct in first half.</title>
<headline>Premier Oil net jumps 87 pct in first half.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.87		   vs 1.17</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 nil		    vs same</p>
<p> Pretax		     27.7		   vs 14.0</p>
<p> Historic cost net	19.1		   vs 10.2</p>
<p> Turnover		   56.9		   vs 36.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Premier Oil Plc said profits rose due to a 31 percent rise in production and a 13 percent rise in oil prices.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 30.9		   vs 16.5</p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Interest charge	  3.0		    vs 2.6</p>
<p> Tax			  8.6		    vs 3.8</p>
<p> Attributable	     19.1		   vs 10.2</p>
<p>Note - Premier said it intends again to recommend a final dividend on the results for the full year. The company said trading in the second half has started well.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
